---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="about — devkage"
  description="About Bona: MSc Computer Science at York, focused on HPC, CUDA, and AI."
>
  <article class="px-5 sm:px-6 py-6 sm:py-8 prose-post">
    <a
      href="/"
      class="inline-block mb-4 font-mono text-[11px] text-[color:var(--color-text-tertiary)] no-underline hover:text-[color:var(--color-accent)]"
    >
      ← back
    </a>

    <h1
      class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight text-[color:var(--color-text-primary)] mb-1"
    >
      About
    </h1>
    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[color:var(--color-text-tertiary)] mb-6">
      who · what · why
    </p>

    <h2>Who</h2>
    <p>
      I'm Bona — Indonesian, Catholic, currently doing an MSc in Computer Science at the
      <strong>University of York</strong>. Before this I shipped commercial software in
      C# and .NET for a few years, mostly backend systems no one will ever see but a lot
      of people depended on.
    </p>

    <h2>What I work on</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>HPC &amp; CUDA</strong> — GPU kernels, profiling, sparse kernels.</li>
      <li><strong>C++</strong> — modern C++, RAII, the bits .NET hid from me for years.</li>
      <li><strong>LLM inference</strong> — KV cache, batching, quantisation. Why decode is slow.</li>
      <li><strong>MPI &amp; distributed compute</strong> — Viking HPC at York.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Why this blog</h2>
    <p>
      I share everything here freely because the resources that helped me the most when I
      was getting started were free, generous, and written by people one step ahead of me.
      I want to be that for someone else.
    </p>
    <p>
      No paywalls. No newsletter funnel. No "10x developer" thinkpieces. Just notes from
      the work, as honest as I can make them.
    </p>

    <h2>Tools I reach for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>C++20, CUDA Toolkit, Python (numpy / PyTorch)</li>
      <li>Linux + zsh + Neovim, mostly</li>
      <li>Viking HPC cluster for the heavy stuff</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Off the keyboard</h2>
    <p>
      Mass on Sundays, long walks along the Ouse, slow cooking, and trying to call home
      more often than I do.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
